A dbt incremental model, showing the pattern that only processes new/changed rows:

```sql
-- models/fct_orders.sql
{{
  config(
    materialized='incremental',
    unique_key='order_id',
    incremental_strategy='merge'
  )
}}

SELECT
  order_id,
  customer_id,
  order_total,
  updated_at
FROM {{ ref('stg_orders') }}

{% if is_incremental() %}
  -- only process rows newer than what's already in this table
  WHERE updated_at > (SELECT max(updated_at) FROM {{ this }})
{% endif %}
```

`is_incremental()` is false on the first run (or a full-refresh), so it builds the whole table. On every subsequent run, it's true, and the model only selects rows newer than what's already there — then dbt merges those rows into the existing table using `order_id` as the unique key, so a re-processed row updates in place rather than duplicating.
